    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0525" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 702.6211/221.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">German Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: In reply to your kind
                    note of the 21st instant, I have the honor most respectfully to say to your
                    excellency that I should be very glad if the case of the Imperial Consul Müller
                    could be discontinued.</p>
                <p>Should your excellency deem it possible to discontinue the case I would be quite
                    ready for my part to take into consideration a transfer of Consul Müller in the
                    way of an exchange of posts with one of the other consuls in the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
